@startuml
title VaultUI Python - Component Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Terminal User" as User

package "vaultui-py.py" {
  component "CLI Parser\nargparse" as CLI
  component "Runtime Config\nflags/env/~/.vaultui.yaml" as Config
  component "VaultTUI\ncurses app controller" as App
  component "Router Stack\nView push/pop/reset" as Router
  component "Views\nDashboard, KV, Policies,\nAuth, PKI, Transit,\nIdentity, DB, AWS" as Views
  component "UI Primitives\nTable, DetailView,\nTextView, Theme, KeyMap" as UI
  component "VaultClient\nurllib HTTP API" as Client
  component "TTLCache\n30s endpoint cache" as Cache
  component "TokenRenewer\nbackground renew-self" as Renewer
  component "Clipboard\nOS copy + auto-clear" as Clipboard
  component "Headless get\nJSON output" as Get
}

cloud "HashiCorp Vault\n/v1 HTTP API" as Vault
database "~/.vaultui.yaml\n~/.vault-token" as Files
collections "OS Clipboard Tools\nxclip/xsel/wl-copy/pbcopy/clip" as ClipboardTools

User --> CLI : starts TUI or get
CLI --> Config : resolves connection
Config --> Files : reads/writes contexts
CLI --> App : interactive mode
CLI --> Get : get subcommand
App --> Router : manages navigation
Router --> Views : current screen
Views --> UI : render and handle keys
Views --> Client : load Vault data
Get --> Client : read resource
Client --> Cache : cache reads
Client --> Vault : GET/LIST/POST
App --> Renewer : starts token renewal
Renewer --> Client : lookup/renew token
Views --> Clipboard : copy values/raw data
Clipboard --> ClipboardTools : write and clear

@enduml
